Ticket #4471 merged every date report into one known issue and named a single fix: the parser
reads the month first, and the tenants write the day first. The desk's own view of the export
has two causes. Each one has its own ticket:

- parser: https://github.com/AdamBurawski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1
- hint: https://github.com/AdamBurawski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2

The counts below are the desk's, from the export.

## Parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped.
This is every report that did not arrive through booking-v3's form. The reports the desk also
reads as a one-day move stay in this count. The desk footnotes them. They are not a third cause.

## Hint

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. The form still reads the date the tenant's
way, day first. People type the order the hint shows. This is a different bug from the parser,
and it only arrives on the form channel. The desk merged these reports into #4471. They are not
that ticket's cause.

